## Definition of done
A feature is done when its entry in ./FEATURES.md is flipped to `passing`
by the evaluator — never by the builder that implemented it. Work
test-first: write the feature's Verify test, then implement until green.

## Commands
- Install: `npm install`
- Build: `npm run build`
- Test (all): `npm test`
- Test (one file): `npm test -- <path>`
- Lint: `npm run lint`
- Dev server: `npm run dev` (http://localhost:3000)

## Architecture
- [src/api/ — route handlers; validate input with zod at the boundary]
- [src/services/ — business logic; no framework imports here]
- [src/db/ — Prisma schema + repositories; services never query directly]
- [tests/ — colocated with source as *.test.ts]

## Conventions
- [TypeScript strict; no `any` without a comment justifying it]
- [Errors: throw AppError subclasses; handlers map them to HTTP responses]
- [Secrets only via environment variables — the commit hook scans for leaks]

## Workflow
- Branch per slice: `feat/<slice-name>`; PRs target `main` (protected).
- Commits are blocked by a hook unless the test suite passes. If blocked,
  fix the failure — do not work around the hook.
- Do not edit FEATURES.md statuses; the evaluator owns them.

## Escalation
Ask the user only for: taste/UX calls the spec doesn't settle, architecture
forks with long-term consequences, missing credentials, or anything that
contradicts SPEC.md. Everything else: decide, note it in the PR description,
move on.
